---
/**
 * Features, written as outcomes rather than a capability list.
 *
 * Everything claimed here must be something the product does or will do. Where
 * something is not built yet it says so — this audience checks, and a carrier
 * who finds one overclaim stops believing the rest.
 */
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro'
import { coverage } from '../lib/site.ts'

const card = 'rounded-xl border border-ink-100 bg-white p-5'

const sections = [
  {
    eyebrow: 'Deadlines',
    title: 'One list, soonest first',
    body: `Every date your fleet has to meet, in one list, with the soonest date first. ${coverage.federal} federal rules that apply wherever you run, and ${coverage.california} California rules on top.`,
    points: [
      ['Drivers, federal', 'Medical certificates, including the shorter 3-month and 1-year cards. CDL expiry. The annual MVR check and the signed review note that goes with it. Clearinghouse queries. And the 30-day limit to get the previous-employer checks on a new driver. These are all federal rules, so they are the same in every state.'],
      ['Trucks', 'The annual DOT inspection and the report you have to keep. Those are federal. In California you also get CVRA weight decals, Clean Truck Check testing windows and the fee that goes with them, and your CHP terminal inspection dates.'],
      ['The carrier', 'MCS-150 update every two years, UCR, Form 2290, operating authority and insurance on file. Those are federal. Then the Motor Carrier Permit, the quarterly fuel-tax return and the apportioned-plate renewal, the way California runs them. Those dates are for carriers based in California, not for other states.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: 'Alerts',
    title: 'Told early, not told all day',
    body: 'Too many alerts are as bad as none. If we write to you all day, you stop reading us. Today we send email. Text messages are not on yet, and we will not sell you something we cannot send.',
    points: [
      ['One email a day, not fourteen', 'Your deadlines come in one email each morning. You do not get a separate email for every item.'],
      ['Your days, your people', 'For each kind of deadline, pick how many days ahead you want to know and who gets the email. Medical cards can go to the office. Authority problems can go to you.'],
      ['Quiet hours', 'Nothing arrives at 2am about a renewal due next month. Urgent items can still come through, and you can see exactly which ones are allowed to.'],
      ['Snooze', 'If you already handled an overdue item, snooze it and it stops asking. We record that you snoozed it and when.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: 'Loads',
    title: 'Booked, dispatched, delivered, paid',
    body: 'Real loads have several stops. The broker load number is not the same as yours. The detention terms are buried in the rate confirmation. We keep all three as fields you can read and search, not as a PDF you have to open again.',
    points: [
      ['Many stops, as standard', 'Pickups, deliveries, drops and hooks in order. Each stop has its own appointment window and its own reference numbers. You also mark if it is a set appointment or first come, first served, because those two go wrong in different ways.'],
      ['Detention terms as fields', 'Free hours, hourly rate, and whether the broker needs to approve it first. That last one is where small carriers lose money.'],
      ['Delivered is not the same as paid', 'The delivery status and the billing status are separate. A load can be delivered and still sitting on an invoice you have not sent, and both screens show it correctly.'],
      ['Search by the broker number', 'The number on the paper in front of you is usually the broker number, not yours. You can search by it.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: 'Dispatch',
    title: 'Dispatch checks the rules for you',
    body: 'Other software at this price does not do this.',
    points: [
      ['It blocks the assignment, it does not write a report', 'If a driver medical card expired last week, you cannot give him a load. You find out while you are making the decision, not in a summary you read next month.'],
      ['Driver, tractor and trailer are separate', 'Trailers get dropped and swapped, and power-only loads use no trailer of yours at all.'],
      ['The server refuses it too', 'The button goes grey, and if the form is forced through anyway, the server says no. Nobody can override this one.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    eyebrow: 'Proof',
    title: 'Something you can hand over',
    body: 'A broker, an insurance company or an officer at a scale asks what you have. You print one dated packet that says what we saw and when.',
    points: [
      ['In the order they read it', 'Driver qualification files in the order 49 CFR 391.51 lists them. Each item is marked present, missing or expired, and the missing ones are listed on the first page.'],
      ['It links to the federal record', 'So the person reading it can check us instead of taking our word.'],
    ],
  },
]

const notYet = [
  // First in the list on purpose. It is the only entry here a buyer could be
  // surprised by after paying, which makes it the one that has to be hardest to
  // miss — the rest of this section is about things nobody expects us to do.
  [
    'State rules outside California',
    `The ${coverage.federal} federal rules apply in every state, and they are most of the list. But California is the only state we have added so far. If your state has its own inspection, permit or filing, it is not in here yet, and we will not suggest that it is. Other states are next. For us a rule is data: the rule number, the schedule, and what proves you did it. So adding a state means adding rules, not building a new product.`,
  ],
  ['We do not read dates from photos', 'A date read wrong and shown as correct is worse than no feature at all. We will add this when checking it is fast.'],
  ['We cannot run your Clearinghouse queries', 'The rules do not allow a service to use your login, and blanket consent is not allowed either. We track when your queries are due and we keep the proof that you ran them.'],
  ['We do not file anything for you', 'We track your dates and we remind you. We are not a law firm and we will not act like one.'],
  ['We are not an ELD, and we do not read one yet', 'You already have one. Keep it. Dispatch here checks dates, not hours of service.'],
]
---

<Public
  title="Features"
  description="Deadline tracking, loads, trips and email alerts for small US trucking fleets. Federal rules in every state, plus the California rules."
>
  <section class="border-b border-ink-100 bg-champagne-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
      <h1 class="max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
        Your deadlines and your loads, in one place.
      </h1>
      {/* ink-700: on `bg-champagne-50`, where ink-500 is 4.30:1. */}
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-700">
        A deadline list only helps you if you open it. So we put it in the same app you use to
        run your loads, and you see both every day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    sections.map((s, i) => (
      <section class:list={['border-b border-ink-100', i % 2 === 1 && 'bg-champagne-50']}>
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium tracking-widest text-brand-600 uppercase">{s.eyebrow}</p>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">{s.title}</h2>
          {/* ink-700: every second section sits on `bg-champagne-50`. */}
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-ink-700">{s.body}</p>
          <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {s.points.map(([t, b]) => (
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink-100 bg-white p-5">
                <p class="font-medium">{t}</p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">{b}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    ))
  }

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">What we do not do</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-ink-500">
      The first one is the edge of what we cover. The rest are things other companies will try
      to sell you.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        notYet.map(([t, b]) => (
          <div class={card}>
            <p class="font-medium">{t}</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">{b}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10">
      {/* Marketing chrome keeps the dark button. */}
      <a href="/check" class="btn btn-dark rounded-xl px-7 py-3.5 font-semibold">
        See your own deadlines →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Public>
